('u', 516, 2078, NULL, NULL, 'The Zephyr is a unique starship design, relying almost entirely on solar winds for sublight propulsion. Super-light sails allow it to ride the torrents of photons streaming through space, and its barebones construction gives it a tiny sensor footprint and almost negligible mass.\n\n\n\nOriginally conceived by the ascetic Intaki polymath Valsas en Dilat as a demonstration of minimalist starship design, it was never intended as a commercial venture. The recent discovery of the uncharted Sleeper Territories and their myriad wormholes has brought the Zephyr new attention - its mass makes it an ideal exploration vessel.\n\n\n\nValsas remains adamant that the Zephyr never sees mass production, but at the close of YC111 he authorized the Intaki Syndicate to distribute a single hull to every registered capsuleer.\n\n\n\nNote: Can fit Prototype Iris Probe Launcher; will not be targeted by Sleeper drones.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 7829060, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
('u', 518, 2082, NULL, 'Hardwiring - Genolution Core Augmentation CA-1', '<br><br><font color="yellow"><b>Traits</b></font><br>Slot 1<br>Boosts perception by 3<br>Provides +1.5% powergrid bonus<br>Provides +1.5% capacitor amount bonus<br>Implant set bonus: 50%<br><br><font color="yellow"><b>Development</b></font><br>The modestly titled ', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 4464.63, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
('u', 2564, 2083, NULL, NULL, 'The Iris system is a prototype launcher designed to work exclusively with the Zephyr exploration platform.\n\n\n\nIts tight integration allows it to work effectively with the minimal power and CPU capacity the Zephyr can provide, but the non-standard interfaces needed for this optimization make it entirely unusable on other ship types.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 6.26325, NULL, 712, NULL, NULL, NULL),
