('u', 4, 21449, NULL, NULL, 'DNA samples are any of various nucleic acids that are usually the molecular basis of heredity, are localized especially in cell nuclei, and are constructed of a double helix held together by hydrogen bonds between purine and pyrimidine bases which project inward from two chains containing alternate links of deoxyribose and phosphate.\n\n\n\nThis DNA sample is taken from the Caldari entrepreneur, Gatti Zhara.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
